.nh
.TH "PB-PORT-NAME-SET" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-port-name-set - Name a machine port


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb port name set <name> <port> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Give a port a name, or move an existing name to another port. With --machine the
address is <name>\&.<machine>\&.<domain>; with --all-machines the name works on every machine
of the active workspace; with --top-level --machine the address is <name>\&.<domain>\&.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--all-machines\fP[=false]
	name this port on every machine of the workspace

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for set

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--machine\fP=""
	the machine whose port is named

.PP
\fB--top-level\fP[=false]
	make <name>\&.<domain> open the port of --machine


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb port name set app 3000 --machine homelab
  pb port name set grafana 3000 --all-machines
  pb port name set jellyfin 8096 --top-level --machine media
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-port-name(1)\fP
